INSERT INTO sat_questions (question_id, external_id, vault_id, disclosed_item_id, source, program, test_type, test_type_desc, domain, primary_class_cd, skill_cd, skill_desc, difficulty, score_band_range_cd, question_type, stimulus_html, stem_html, answer_options, correct_answer, answer_keys, rationale_html, correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale, image_count, parent_template_name, parent_template_id, template_cluster_id, template_cluster_name, origin, position, answer_style, section, raw_payload, created_date, updated_date) VALUES
    ($SATQ$24014c3f$SATQ$, $SATQ$16d68a8e-72f4-4437-896b-53aed15d3c95$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$22a130f6-158b-4824-945b-b2a49533fc44$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Severo Ochoa discovered the enzyme PNPase in 1955.</li>
<li>PNPase is involved in both the creation and degradation of mRNA.</li>
<li>Ochoa incorrectly hypothesized that PNPase provides the genetic blueprints for mRNA.</li>
<li>The discovery of PNPase proved critical to deciphering the human genetic code.</li>
<li>Deciphering the genetic code has led to a better understanding of how genetic variations affect human health.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize the significance of Ochoa&rsquo;s discovery. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2e22ea96-3762-4850-82f7-7dce8f5b754d","content":"<p>Ochoa&rsquo;s 1955 discovery of PNPase proved critical to deciphering the human genetic code, leading to a better understanding of how genetic variations affect human health.</p>"},{"id":"edd83d61-d194-4ffb-984e-b61876fd234b","content":"<p>Ochoa first discovered PNPase, an enzyme that he hypothesized contained the genetic blueprints for mRNA, in 1955.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"d30d4092-751b-430d-ba8e-0e4d0d4febc7","content":"<p>In 1955, Ochoa discovered the PNPase enzyme, which is involved in both the creation and degradation of mRNA.</p>"},{"id":"6e98f827-a520-4598-ba7a-2b808bc565d4","content":"<p>Though his discovery of PNPase was critical to deciphering the human genetic code, Ochoa incorrectly hypothesized that the enzyme was the source of mRNA&rsquo;s genetic blueprints.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2e22ea96-3762-4850-82f7-7dce8f5b754d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes the significance of Ochoa&rsquo;s discovery, noting that it proved critical to deciphering the human genetic code, which resulted in a better understanding of how genetic variations affect human health. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence explains what Ochoa discovered, it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the significance of the discovery. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence explains what Ochoa discovered, it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the significance of the discovery. Choice D is incorrect. While the sentence mentions that Ochoa&rsquo;s discovery was crucial, it emphasizes Ochoa&rsquo;s incorrect hypothesis, not the significance of the discovery. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-772-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$59a929be-5812-4c7c-810c-fb361f6c2279$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"24014c3f","external_id":"16d68a8e-72f4-4437-896b-53aed15d3c95","vaultid":"22a130f6-158b-4824-945b-b2a49533fc44","uId":"6ae1f662-4157-4f06-b5e8-04277aecdc42","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Severo Ochoa discovered the enzyme PNPase in 1955.</li>\n<li>PNPase is involved in both the creation and degradation of mRNA.</li>\n<li>Ochoa incorrectly hypothesized that PNPase provides the genetic blueprints for mRNA.</li>\n<li>The discovery of PNPase proved critical to deciphering the human genetic code.</li>\n<li>Deciphering the genetic code has led to a better understanding of how genetic variations affect human health.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize the significance of Ochoa&rsquo;s discovery. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2e22ea96-3762-4850-82f7-7dce8f5b754d","content":"<p>Ochoa&rsquo;s 1955 discovery of PNPase proved critical to deciphering the human genetic code, leading to a better understanding of how genetic variations affect human health.</p>"},{"id":"edd83d61-d194-4ffb-984e-b61876fd234b","content":"<p>Ochoa first discovered PNPase, an enzyme that he hypothesized contained the genetic blueprints for mRNA, in 1955.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"d30d4092-751b-430d-ba8e-0e4d0d4febc7","content":"<p>In 1955, Ochoa discovered the PNPase enzyme, which is involved in both the creation and degradation of mRNA.</p>"},{"id":"6e98f827-a520-4598-ba7a-2b808bc565d4","content":"<p>Though his discovery of PNPase was critical to deciphering the human genetic code, Ochoa incorrectly hypothesized that the enzyme was the source of mRNA&rsquo;s genetic blueprints.</p>"}],"keys":["2e22ea96-3762-4850-82f7-7dce8f5b754d"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes the significance of Ochoa&rsquo;s discovery, noting that it proved critical to deciphering the human genetic code, which resulted in a better understanding of how genetic variations affect human health. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence explains what Ochoa discovered, it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the significance of the discovery. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence explains what Ochoa discovered, it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the significance of the discovery. Choice D is incorrect. While the sentence mentions that Ochoa&rsquo;s discovery was crucial, it emphasizes Ochoa&rsquo;s incorrect hypothesis, not the significance of the discovery. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-772-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"59a929be-5812-4c7c-810c-fb361f6c2279","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959352,"updateDate":1691007959352}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959352, 1691007959352),
    ($SATQ$249508d9$SATQ$, $SATQ$442ba363-c324-4677-a1b4-a634b4191a8d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>With his room-sized installation <em>Unicorn/My Private Sky</em>, Norwegian artist B&oslash;rre S&aelig;thre succeeds in creating a whimsical yet perplexing experience. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> when visitors set foot inside the fantastically blue room and encounter the life-sized stuffed unicorn preening at the far end of it, they are both dazzled and confused&mdash;as if stepping into a strange and enchanting new world.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"8abbd44f-b631-4fd3-8ed8-2b60aaca52c7","content":"<p>Second,</p>"},{"id":"1e466846-88c1-4812-b531-482f356489f9","content":"<p>Instead,</p>"},{"id":"6f7ffff0-6be5-48c0-bbee-220d45c2634a","content":"<p>Indeed,</p>"},{"id":"910d88b6-df4d-4015-bc4f-9837efc2b19d","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6f7ffff0-6be5-48c0-bbee-220d45c2634a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. "Indeed" logically signals that the description of the art installation in this sentence&mdash;its blue room and preening unicorn that leave visitors "dazzled and confused"&mdash;offers additional emphasis in support of the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the installation&rsquo;s "whimsical yet perplexing experience."</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because "second" illogically signals that the description in this sentence is a second, separate claim from the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the installation&rsquo;s "whimsical yet perplexing experience." Instead, the specific details describing the installation emphasize and support the previous claim. Choice B is incorrect because "instead" illogically signals that the description in this sentence is an alternative to the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the installation&rsquo;s "whimsical yet perplexing experience." Rather, the specific details describing the installation emphasize and support that claim. Choice D is incorrect because "nevertheless" illogically signals that the description in this sentence is true despite the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the installation&rsquo;s "whimsical yet perplexing experience." Instead, the specific details describing the installation emphasize and support that claim.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"249508d9","external_id":"442ba363-c324-4677-a1b4-a634b4191a8d","vaultid":null,"uId":"895f1a38-cbdd-474b-9a46-308d12eb8ab4","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>With his room-sized installation <em>Unicorn/My Private Sky</em>, Norwegian artist B&oslash;rre S&aelig;thre succeeds in creating a whimsical yet perplexing experience. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> when visitors set foot inside the fantastically blue room and encounter the life-sized stuffed unicorn preening at the far end of it, they are both dazzled and confused&mdash;as if stepping into a strange and enchanting new world.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"8abbd44f-b631-4fd3-8ed8-2b60aaca52c7","content":"<p>Second,</p>"},{"id":"1e466846-88c1-4812-b531-482f356489f9","content":"<p>Instead,</p>"},{"id":"6f7ffff0-6be5-48c0-bbee-220d45c2634a","content":"<p>Indeed,</p>"},{"id":"910d88b6-df4d-4015-bc4f-9837efc2b19d","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"}],"keys":["6f7ffff0-6be5-48c0-bbee-220d45c2634a"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. \"Indeed\" logically signals that the description of the art installation in this sentence&mdash;its blue room and preening unicorn that leave visitors \"dazzled and confused\"&mdash;offers additional emphasis in support of the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the installation&rsquo;s \"whimsical yet perplexing experience.\"</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because \"second\" illogically signals that the description in this sentence is a second, separate claim from the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the installation&rsquo;s \"whimsical yet perplexing experience.\" Instead, the specific details describing the installation emphasize and support the previous claim. Choice B is incorrect because \"instead\" illogically signals that the description in this sentence is an alternative to the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the installation&rsquo;s \"whimsical yet perplexing experience.\" Rather, the specific details describing the installation emphasize and support that claim. Choice D is incorrect because \"nevertheless\" illogically signals that the description in this sentence is true despite the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the installation&rsquo;s \"whimsical yet perplexing experience.\" Instead, the specific details describing the installation emphasize and support that claim.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669206,"updateDate":1743430669206}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669206, 1743430669206),
    ($SATQ$25361ec6$SATQ$, $SATQ$277fb947-e7d2-4316-bcef-a79554eb9a08$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Scientists long debated the origins of chondrules, tiny glass beads that formed in meteors billions of years ago. For decades, different theories were proposed, from lightning strikes to powerful rock collisions, but none had sufficient evidentiary support. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> scientists found strong evidence that chondrules were formed by shock waves in nearby nebulae.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9c1df694-6163-412b-a9df-51127796e5ef","content":"<p>For example,</p>"},{"id":"e1c9678b-812e-4035-a965-0d39735da691","content":"<p>Therefore,</p>"},{"id":"1c4768d9-9837-4462-a4fe-b697bb501830","content":"<p>Similarly,</p>"},{"id":"201e3cd1-0f7d-4c8d-843b-bbc242c2a966","content":"<p>Finally,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["201e3cd1-0f7d-4c8d-843b-bbc242c2a966"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. "Finally" logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that scientists found evidence that chondrules were formed by shock waves in nearby nebulae&mdash;indicates a conclusion to the scientific debate mentioned in the previous sentences.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because "for example" illogically signals that the information about the evidence for chondrule formation in this sentence exemplifies the information about the scientific debate regarding chondrule formation in the previous sentences. Instead, it indicates a conclusion to the debate. Choice B is incorrect because "therefore" illogically signals that the information in this sentence is a result of the previous information about the scientific debate regarding chondrule formation. Instead, it indicates a conclusion to the debate. Choice C is incorrect because "similarly" illogically signals that the information that follows is similar to the information about the scientific debate regarding chondrule formation in the previous sentences. Instead, it indicates a conclusion to the debate.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"25361ec6","external_id":"277fb947-e7d2-4316-bcef-a79554eb9a08","vaultid":null,"uId":"3880cf04-ca34-4417-9eea-1097b09037a7","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Scientists long debated the origins of chondrules, tiny glass beads that formed in meteors billions of years ago. For decades, different theories were proposed, from lightning strikes to powerful rock collisions, but none had sufficient evidentiary support. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> scientists found strong evidence that chondrules were formed by shock waves in nearby nebulae.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"9c1df694-6163-412b-a9df-51127796e5ef","content":"<p>For example,</p>"},{"id":"e1c9678b-812e-4035-a965-0d39735da691","content":"<p>Therefore,</p>"},{"id":"1c4768d9-9837-4462-a4fe-b697bb501830","content":"<p>Similarly,</p>"},{"id":"201e3cd1-0f7d-4c8d-843b-bbc242c2a966","content":"<p>Finally,</p>"}],"keys":["201e3cd1-0f7d-4c8d-843b-bbc242c2a966"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. \"Finally\" logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that scientists found evidence that chondrules were formed by shock waves in nearby nebulae&mdash;indicates a conclusion to the scientific debate mentioned in the previous sentences.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because \"for example\" illogically signals that the information about the evidence for chondrule formation in this sentence exemplifies the information about the scientific debate regarding chondrule formation in the previous sentences. Instead, it indicates a conclusion to the debate. Choice B is incorrect because \"therefore\" illogically signals that the information in this sentence is a result of the previous information about the scientific debate regarding chondrule formation. Instead, it indicates a conclusion to the debate. Choice C is incorrect because \"similarly\" illogically signals that the information that follows is similar to the information about the scientific debate regarding chondrule formation in the previous sentences. Instead, it indicates a conclusion to the debate.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323042,"updateDate":1730147323042}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323042, 1730147323042),
    ($SATQ$25755def$SATQ$, $SATQ$49237e71-5dc2-4099-b224-9250cc0fa6c8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Generally, an object will heat up when twisted.</li>
<li>The twisting of an object is known as torsion.</li>
<li>A 2019 study led by Zunfeng Liu and Ray Baughman tested the torsional heating of various fibers.</li>
<li>When a 3-millimeter-thick sample of thermoplastic polyurethane (TPU) fiber was twisted, its average surface temperature increased by 6&deg;C.</li>
<li>When a 4-millimeter-thick sample of styrene-ethylene-butylene-styrene (SEBS) rubber fiber was twisted, its average surface temperature increased by 3.5&deg;C.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to contrast the two samples. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"546d840e-9990-43a4-b468-ea74e3c28fa0","content":"<p>When the fibers were twisted as part of the 2019 study, the surface temperature of both samples increased.</p>"},{"id":"8d68bd81-7b9b-4346-9733-a8a06234095a","content":"<p>In 2019, researchers studied the effect of torsional heating on various fibers, including samples of SEBS rubber and TPU.</p>"},{"id":"efa4a24c-60ea-43fa-83e4-c7eda4f07396","content":"<p>Twisting an object will generally cause its temperature to increase, a process known as torsional heating.</p>"},{"id":"4837a988-f4ac-490a-b0eb-98aba2505f72","content":"<p>The SEBS rubber sample used in the 2019 study was thicker than the TPU sample.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4837a988-f4ac-490a-b0eb-98aba2505f72"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence contrasts the two samples, noting that the SEBS rubber sample, at 4 millimeters thick, was thicker than the TPU sample, which was 3 millimeters thick.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the sentence mentions a similarity between the TPU fiber and the SEBS rubber; it doesn&rsquo;t  contrast the two samples. Choice B is incorrect because the sentence indicates that both the SEBS rubber and TPU samples were part of the 2019 study; it doesn&rsquo;t contrast the two samples. Choice C is incorrect because the sentence describes the process of torsional heating; it doesn&rsquo;t contrast the two samples.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"25755def","external_id":"49237e71-5dc2-4099-b224-9250cc0fa6c8","vaultid":null,"uId":"8dd082df-ecfb-4dcd-8298-63e9d581a1ae","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Generally, an object will heat up when twisted.</li>\n<li>The twisting of an object is known as torsion.</li>\n<li>A 2019 study led by Zunfeng Liu and Ray Baughman tested the torsional heating of various fibers.</li>\n<li>When a 3-millimeter-thick sample of thermoplastic polyurethane (TPU) fiber was twisted, its average surface temperature increased by 6&deg;C.</li>\n<li>When a 4-millimeter-thick sample of styrene-ethylene-butylene-styrene (SEBS) rubber fiber was twisted, its average surface temperature increased by 3.5&deg;C.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to contrast the two samples. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?&nbsp;</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"546d840e-9990-43a4-b468-ea74e3c28fa0","content":"<p>When the fibers were twisted as part of the 2019 study, the surface temperature of both samples increased.</p>"},{"id":"8d68bd81-7b9b-4346-9733-a8a06234095a","content":"<p>In 2019, researchers studied the effect of torsional heating on various fibers, including samples of SEBS rubber and TPU.</p>"},{"id":"efa4a24c-60ea-43fa-83e4-c7eda4f07396","content":"<p>Twisting an object will generally cause its temperature to increase, a process known as torsional heating.</p>"},{"id":"4837a988-f4ac-490a-b0eb-98aba2505f72","content":"<p>The SEBS rubber sample used in the 2019 study was thicker than the TPU sample.</p>"}],"keys":["4837a988-f4ac-490a-b0eb-98aba2505f72"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence contrasts the two samples, noting that the SEBS rubber sample, at 4 millimeters thick, was thicker than the TPU sample, which was 3 millimeters thick.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the sentence mentions a similarity between the TPU fiber and the SEBS rubber; it doesn&rsquo;t  contrast the two samples. Choice B is incorrect because the sentence indicates that both the SEBS rubber and TPU samples were part of the 2019 study; it doesn&rsquo;t contrast the two samples. Choice C is incorrect because the sentence describes the process of torsional heating; it doesn&rsquo;t contrast the two samples.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061177,"updateDate":1755117061177}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061177, 1755117061177),
    ($SATQ$259d16ac$SATQ$, $SATQ$b7fbabac-300e-4bf8-84bc-4e099b7b1f09$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In 1859, the novel <em>Adam Bede </em>was published in England.</li>
<li>According to the novel&rsquo;s title page, the author&rsquo;s name was George Eliot.</li>
<li>George Eliot was widely assumed to be a pseudonym.</li>
<li>A pseudonym is a fake name used to conceal an author&rsquo;s identity.</li>
<li>A woman named Mary Ann Evans later revealed herself as the novel&rsquo;s real author.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to identify the real author of <em>Adam Bede</em>. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"92571fa5-b51e-4498-b3b6-583618fc021f","content":"<p>The real author of <em>Adam Bede </em>was Mary Ann Evans<em>, </em>who published the novel using the pseudonym<em>&nbsp;</em>George Eliot.</p>"},{"id":"a7a0f49c-0079-439f-8177-e9d4de96f169","content":"<p>George Eliot, which <em>Adam Bede</em>&rsquo;s<em> </em>title page indicated was the name of the novel&rsquo;s author, was widely assumed to be a pseudonym.</p>"},{"id":"b9705af3-280d-43c7-b05e-deca5ffe8dfe","content":"<p>The title page of the novel <em>Adam Bede</em> indicated that the author&rsquo;s name was George Eliot.</p>"},{"id":"a0dff8dd-cbfd-41e5-8069-9aef2a5395b0","content":"<p>A woman who had used a pseudonym to conceal her identity later revealed herself as the real author of <em>Adam Bede.</em></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["92571fa5-b51e-4498-b3b6-583618fc021f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence identifies the novel&rsquo;s real author, explaining that Mary Ann Evans published the novel under the pseudonym of George Eliot.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. The sentence explains that George Eliot was assumed to be a pseudonym; it doesn&rsquo;t identify the novel&rsquo;s real author. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence specifies the pseudonym used on the novel&rsquo;s title page; it doesn&rsquo;t identify the novel&rsquo;s real author. Choice D is incorrect. While the sentence indicates that the novel&rsquo;s real author used a pseudonym, it doesn&rsquo;t identify that author as Mary Ann Evans.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"259d16ac","external_id":"b7fbabac-300e-4bf8-84bc-4e099b7b1f09","vaultid":null,"uId":"c078a024-7aff-40ea-8ecf-b4497c3720b3","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_de