which of the three foods has the highest magnesium content.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061192,"updateDate":1755117061192}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061192, 1755117061192),
    ($SATQ$25adba4e$SATQ$, $SATQ$0f25a5ee-f1f8-494b-8e6f-58f5d6f7ce7b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In 1897, twenty Black US Army infantrymen rode bicycles from Montana to Missouri.</li>
<li>The 1,900-mile journey took forty-one days.</li>
<li>The goal was to test the idea of forming a military bicycle corps.</li>
<li>In 2022, Erick Cede&ntilde;o, a Black long-distance cyclist, reenacted the journey.</li>
<li>Cede&ntilde;o wanted to honor the infantrymen on the journey&rsquo;s 125th anniversary.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize how far the infantrymen traveled. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"19d146bf-06a4-491d-becb-77691c28d006","content":"<p>The US infantrymen rode their bicycles from Montana to Missouri&mdash;traveling a total of 1,900 miles.</p>"},{"id":"caa6c98e-d6cb-4429-94ae-c92ef5f78d9e","content":"<p>The 125th anniversary of the infantrymen&rsquo;s journey was in 2022.</p>"},{"id":"c81a12ba-9fd4-44d3-97e6-494c315d1528","content":"<p>The goal of the 1897 journey was to test the idea of forming a military bicycle corps.</p>"},{"id":"f8f94bb7-19d9-48b2-8d2a-c890675db5a8","content":"<p>Over a century later, Erick Cede&ntilde;o honored the infantrymen by reenacting their 1897 journey.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["19d146bf-06a4-491d-becb-77691c28d006"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes how far the infantrymen traveled, indicating that they rode their bicycles from Montana to Missouri, a total of 1,900 miles.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because the sentence mentions when the anniversary of the journey occurred; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize how far the infantrymen traveled. Choice C is incorrect because the sentence discusses the goal of the journey; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize how far the infantrymen traveled. Choice D is incorrect because the sentence notes that Cede&ntilde;o honored the infantrymen by reenacting their journey; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize how far the infantrymen traveled.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"25adba4e","external_id":"0f25a5ee-f1f8-494b-8e6f-58f5d6f7ce7b","vaultid":null,"uId":"ed481a9e-34c4-46fd-8813-9a3650cbbc15","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty"